    {
      "id": "p0124-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Stop signs are red in Japan too, so this hint would be easy to translate into Japanese without any major issues. However, the translator felt the information would \"click\" more naturally in Japanese if it referred to a stoplight instead of a stop sign. Thus the line became:",
        "raw": "Stop signs are red in Japan too, so this hint would be easy to translate\ninto Japanese without any major issues. However, the translator felt the\ninformation would \"click\" more naturally in Japanese if it referred to a\nstoplight instead of a stop sign. Thus the line became:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29398032,
          0.38044286,
          0.84591901,
          0.44883571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29113406,
          0.37972857,
          0.89177532,
          0.44990714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          22,
          23,
          24,
          25
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "日本的停车标志也是红色，因此这条提示直接翻成日语也不会有什么大问题。不过，译者觉得，用交通信号灯代替停车标志，日本玩家会更容易“明白过来”。于是台词变成了：",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.29350084,
          0.37901429,
          0.889735,
          0.45240714
