    {
      "id": "p0124-b010",
      "kind": "quote",
      "source": {
        "text": "On a slightly different note, this whole blue/green issue is a common challenge when translating between Japanese and English. One time, I had to translate a Japanese anime script without any video to check, so I basically had to guess a color and hope it was right. Later, when I saw the final product, I was relieved to see that my guess was right.",
        "raw": "On a slightly different note, this whole blue/green issue is a common\nchallenge when translating between Japanese and English. One time, I\nhad to translate a Japanese anime script without any video to check, so I\nbasically had to guess a color and hope it was right. Later, when I saw the\nfinal product, I was relieved to see that my guess was right.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.31289414,
          0.81522143,
          0.8709436,
          0.88761429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.31156793,
          0.81450714,
          0.87226981,
          0.88868571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          40,
          41,
          42,
          43,
          44
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "稍微岔开一下，蓝色与绿色的区别是日英翻译中的常见难题。有一次，我翻译日本动画剧本时没有视频可核对，只能基本靠猜颜色，祈祷自己猜对。后来看到成片，发现没猜错，才松了口气。",
        "status": "draft",
